@H1 12. SCALING, GLOBAL COMPATIBILITY, FUTURE-PROOFING
@H2 12.1 Scaling
@P Growth step is one cell ({{res.synergy.growth_step_pop|,.0f}} people); every cell is self-contained for water, power and waste, so per-capita performance does not degrade as wards are added. Sweep of density and cell size around the adopted design:
{{table:sweep}}
@P The adopted point (apothem 300 m, 90 p/ha) lies on the plateau and at the edge of feasibility: cells above 300 m break the 400 m access gate; density above ~100 p/ha breaks canopy, fresh-food, drought and conflict gates.
@H2 12.2 Global compatibility: site adapter (5 climates x matching hazard profiles)
{{table:adapter}}
@P Lisbon fails G16 at both baseline and tuned: at latitude 38.7 deg winter sun is low, so lanes must be 2 storeys or wider (L-15). Other sites pass after automatic lever tuning, showing the design is parametric, not site-bound. Hemisphere and latitude flip sun side, PV tilt and winter-sun spacing automatically.
@H2 12.3 Future-proofing
@L 100% spare microducts and a spare wet-strip bay (thermal loop, hydrogen-ready is NOT assumed); DC bus option; colonnade line reserved for pole-rail freight; 8 m x 8 m landing reservations at ward nodes (T3, zero dependency); cell battery interface = AequPack; open standards at every interface; annual re-run of the model with fresh climate data.
@H1 13. OPTIBEST VERIFICATION REPORT
@H2 13.1 Iteration ladder (cumulative; every row re-runs all gates)
{{table:ladder}}
@P Result: composite {{an.ladder.0.composite|.3f}} (I0, v1.0 re-evaluated) -> {{an.ladder.7.composite|.3f}} (final); gates {{an.ladder.0.gates_ok}}/{{an.ladder.0.gates_n}} -> {{an.ladder.7.gates_ok}}/{{an.ladder.7.gates_n}}. Largest single gains: hex layout (+{{an.ladder.1.delta|.3f}}), unified corridors (+{{an.ladder.4.delta|.3f}}), sponge drainage (+{{an.ladder.3.delta|.3f}}).
