@H2 13.4 Plateau verification (five methods)
@P METHOD 1 - MULTI-ATTEMPT ENHANCEMENT SEEKING (4 distinct searches over 10 priced levers; unpriced levers fixed and documented):
{{table:plateau}}
@BLOCK METHOD 2 - INDEPENDENT PERSPECTIVES
EXPERT (civil/urban): layout, SuDS, microgrid, corridor logic sound; wants event-scale hydrology + hourly energy study (L-02, L-05). RESIDENT: 5-minute walks, shade, hygiene hubs; reclaimed-water acceptance needs co-design (risk register). MANUFACTURER: materials local except PV/batteries (priority I-1). MAINTAINER: troughs + liftable pavers + common tools; crews computed (7.8). ADVERSARY: stress table defines the envelope; cyber and wildfire have mitigations. PLANET: P-loop, recovery, nature, canopy pass; carbon-negative NOT verified (O-05). RESULT: PASS WITH CONDITIONS (documented).
@END
@BLOCK METHOD 3 - ALTERNATIVE ARCHITECTURE
Concentric-radial vs hex (4.1), piped vs sponge (I3), separate vs unified corridors (I4), deep tunnels vs trough (I4): the adopted architecture is superior on every computed KPI. RESULT: PASS.
@END
@P METHOD 4 - THEORETICAL LIMIT COMPARISON (gaps explained):
{{table:limits_theory}}
@BLOCK METHOD 5 - FRESH RE-EVALUATION
Re-run in a clean process: python -m efe_city check gives {{d.gates_ok}}/{{d.gates_n}}; this document regenerates with identical numbers; adversarial review of every claim against model output found no further model-space enhancement. RESULT: PASS (model space); field items remain open.
@END
@H2 13.5 Anti-gaming (4.6)
@P (a) The first gap pass found gaps, so the second-angle pass was mandatory and run (13.2). (b) Every certification field cites a computed value or test; assertions are void. (c) Plateau is not claimed for schedule reasons: field gates stay open (13.7).
