@H1 14. DEV POLICY AND MODEL MANUAL
@BLOCK PACKAGE efe_city_model/  (stdlib Python 3.12, no dependencies)
efe_city/core.py site.py urban.py resources.py resilience.py synergy.py economics.py evaluate.py analysis.py drawings.py report.py tables.py content.py cli.py | configs/*.json | data/*.json | templates/*.odf | tests/test_model.py
COMMANDS: python -m efe_city run|check|analyze|draw|build [--config F] [--set key=json] [--out DIR]
EXAMPLES: --set geometry.gross_density_p_ha=80 ; --set site.climate=\"lisbon\" --set site.hazard_profile=\"lisbon\"
TESTS: python -m unittest discover -s tests   (mass + energy closure, geometry, hazards, report)
@END
@L EXTENSIBLE: add a subsystem with @subsystem(name, needs=...); add a KPI to SPEC; add a table with @table_fn; add a site by adding JSON.
@L MODULAR + SCRIPTABLE + AUTOMATABLE: every module is a pure function of config; CLI exit codes (check returns 1 on any failed gate) fit CI. HUMAN + AGENT FRIENDLY: JSON in/out, dotted-path overrides, deterministic seeds, loud errors. REPLICABLE: one command regenerates numbers, drawings, blueprint and photo prompt.
